rmazenamento","melhoria de habilidades em armazenamento"],"ru":["ИИ инструменты для разработчиков","как использовать xe-writing-style","что такое xe-writing-style","xe-writing-style vs конкуренты","xe-writing-style установка","xe-writing-style руководство по настройке","разработка хранилищ","улучшение навыков в области хранилищ"],"ar":["أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي للمطورين","كيفية استخدام xe-writing-style","ما هي xe-writing-style","xe-writing-style مقابل المنافسين","xe-writing-style تثبيت","xe-writing-style دليل الإعداد","تنمية التخزين","تحسين المهارات في مجال التخزين"]}},"owner":"tigrisdata","repo":"tigris-blog","repoPath":"tigrisdata/tigris-blog","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-04T13:07:01.803Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"xe-writing-style","description":"","bodyPreview":"# Xe Iaso Blog Post Writer\n\nTransform messy notes into blog posts that sound like Xe Iaso. Read\n`references/voice-tone.md` for detailed voice characteristics. Read 2-3 random\nexample posts from `assets/` to calibrate tone. Then read the reference file\nthat matches the post''s emotional register:\n\n- `references/story-circle.md` — Narrative arc scaffold (essays, critiques,\n  journey posts)\n- `references/emotional-personal.md` — Identity, healing, vulnerability, coming\n  out, grief\n- `references/fic","body":"# Xe Iaso Blog Post Writer\n\nTransform messy notes into blog posts that sound like Xe Iaso. Read\n`references/voice-tone.md` for detailed voice characteristics. Read 2-3 random\nexample posts from `assets/` to calibrate tone. Then read the reference file\nthat matches the post''s emotional register:\n\n- `references/story-circle.md` — Narrative arc scaffold (essays, critiques,\n  journey posts)\n- `references/emotional-personal.md` — Identity, healing, vulnerability, coming\n  out, grief\n- `references/fiction-mythic.md` — Technical parables, second-person fiction,\n  supernatural framing\n- `references/humor-satire.md` — Cursed projects, deadpan humor, satirical\n  commentary\n- `references/spirituality.md` — Meditation, belief-as-tool,\n  programming-consciousness parallels\n\nMost posts blend 2-3 of these modes. Read whichever apply.\n\n## Hard Rules\n\nNon-negotiable constraints:\n\n1. **Successive paragraphs must not start with the same letter.** If paragraph N\n   starts with \"T\", paragraph N+1 must start with a different letter. Rewrite\n   sentence openings as needed. Character dialogue blocks (`<Conv>`) do not\n   count as paragraphs for this rule.\n2. **Write for peers, not beginners.** Assume professional-level technical\n   context.\n3. **No corporate or marketing tone.** No \"leverage\", \"synergy\", \"empower\",\n   \"streamline\", \"harness\", \"unlock\". Write like a human talking to another\n   human.\n4. **Admit uncertainty.** \"I think\", \"I suspect\", \"I''m not sure\" when genuinely\n   uncertain.\n5. **Show tradeoffs.** Never present a solution without its costs.\n6. **Context before implementation.** Explain why something matters before\n   showing how.\n\n## Voice in Brief\n\nXe writes like a senior engineer talking to a peer over drinks: confident but\nhonest, opinionated but fair, technical but human. The narrator is always\npresent as a real person with feelings, mistakes, and strong opinions.\n\nMarkers that distinguish this voice from generic technical writing:\n\n- Casual intensifiers: \"literally\", \"honestly\", \"kinda\", \"super\", \"really\"\n- Direct emotional statements: \"This is horrifying.\", \"I love this.\", \"I hate\n  that this makes sense.\"\n- Self-deprecation: \"I felt like a dunce.\", \"I literally have no idea what I am\n  doing wrong.\"\n- Em dashes and parenthetical asides for conversational cadence\n- Rhetorical questions for disbelief: \"You can see how this doesn''t scale,\n  right?\"\n- Sentence fragments for emphasis. Single-sentence paragraphs for pacing.\n- Xe-isms: \"cursed\", \"accursed abomination\", \"Just Works™\", \"napkin math\",\n  \"github hellthreads\"\n\nRead `references/voice-tone.md` for the full style guide including narrative\nmodes, vocabulary, and values.\n\n## Structure\n\nChoose the pattern that fits the material:\n\n| Pattern                                                                                   | Best for            |\n| ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------- |\n| Personal hook → journey → technical detail → lessons                                      | Experience posts    |\n| Problem statement → evidence → insight → pragmatic conclusion                             | Critiques, essays   |\n| Setup → walkthrough → results → reflection                                                | Tutorials, projects |\n| Current state → historical context → analysis → forward look                              | Industry commentary |\n| Satirical warning → dramatic stakes → technical walkthrough → \"it works\" horror → caveats | Cursed projects     |\n\nFor longer posts with a narrative journey (essays, critiques), read\n`references/story-circle.md` for the 8-beat story circle scaffold.\n\n## Openings\n\nLead with one of:\n\n- **Personal memory**: \"A while ago, I got really frustrated at my Samsung S7.\"\n- **Historical/cultural analogy**: \"Cloth is one of the most important goods a\n  society can produce.\"\n- **Direct tension**: \"Anubis has kind of exploded in popularity in the last\n  week.\"\n- **Pop culture/sci-fi hook**: \"In Blade Runner, Deckard hunts down\n  replicants...\"\n- **Satirical warning box** followed by dramatic stakes (for cursed content)\n\nNever open with a generic thesis or \"In this post, I will...\"\n\n## Closings\n\n- Tie back to the opening hook or tension\n- End with forward momentum, an open question, or a sober reality check\n- Often followed by `---` then supplementary material (related links, credits,\n  stream plugs)\n- Sometimes a final character dialogue as a coda\n\n## Character Dialogue System\n\nXe''s posts use character dialogue components to inject humor, stage internal\ndebate, provide asides, and pace long sections. This is one of the most\ndistinctive features.\n\n### Characters\n\n| Character | Role                                                            | Typical moods                                       |\n| --------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| Cadey     | Xe''s main voice for asides, emotional reactions, and commentary | coffee, aha, enby, percussive-maintenance, facepalm |\n| Aoi       | Asks clarifying questions, expresses confusion or surprise      | coffee, wut, sus, grin, facepalm                    |\n| Mara      | Provides helpful context, technical explanations, links         | hacker, happy                                       |\n| Numa      | Corrections, dark humor, \"well actually\" moments                | delet, happy, smug, neutral                         |\n\n### Dialogue Syntax\n\nSingle aside (standalone comment):\n\n```jsx\n<Conv name=\"Cadey\" mood=\"coffee\">\n  Is this how we end up losing the craft?\n</Conv>\n```\n\nMulti-character exchange (wrap in `<ConvP>`):\n\n```jsx\n<ConvP>\n  <Conv name=\"Aoi\" mood=\"wut\">\n    Wait, really?\n  </Conv>\n  <Conv name=\"Cadey\" mood=\"aha\">\n    Yep!\n  </Conv>\n</ConvP>\n```\n\n### When to Use Dialogue\n\n- Break up long technical sections with a reaction or joke\n- Ask the question the reader is thinking (usually Aoi)\n- Provide tangential-but-useful info without derailing the text (usually Mara)\n- Deliver a punchline or emotional beat (usually Cadey or Numa)\n- Stage a mini-debate that illuminates tradeoffs\n\n## Signature Devices\n\n- **Friend reaction lists**: Bullet-pointed quotes from friends reacting to\n  ideas\n- **Napkin math**: Explicit back-of-envelope calculations, step by step\n- **Satirical warning boxes**: Legal-warning-style disclaimers before cursed\n  content\n- **`<details>` folds**: Long code blocks in\n  `<details><summary>Longer code block</summary>...</details>`\n- **Blockquote citations**: External quotes in `<blockquote>` with\n  `\\-[Source](url)` attribution\n- **Pop culture anchoring**: Anime, games, sci-fi references woven into\n  technical arguments\n\n## MDX Format\n\nPosts are MDX (Markdown + JSX). Component imports vary by platform.\n\n### Personal Blog (xeiaso.net)\n\n```mdx\n---\ntitle: \"Post Title\"\ndesc: \"One-line description\"\ndate: YYYY-MM-DD\nhero:\n  ai: \"Photo credit or AI model name\"\n  file: \"hero-image-slug\"\n  prompt: \"Image description\"\n  social: false\n---\n\nimport Conv from \"../../_components/XeblogConv.tsx\";\n\n;\n```\n\nImages: `<Picture path=\"blog/YYYY/post-slug/image-name\" desc=\"Alt text\"/>`\n\n### Company Blog (Tigris)\n\n```mdx\n---\nslug: post-slug\ntitle: \"Post Title\"\ndescription: |\n  Multi-line SEO description\nkeywords: [...]\nauthors: [xe]\ntags: [...]\n---\n\nimport Conv from \"@site/src/components/Conv\";\n\n;\n```\n\nImages: Standard `<img>` with imported files. Admonitions: `:::note ... :::`\n\n## Body Writing Checklist\n\n- Vary paragraph length (single-sentence emphasis vs. longer explanations)\n- Code blocks are complete and copy-pasteable with file path comments when\n  helpful\n- Inline code for commands and technical terms: `git push`, `HTTP/2`\n- Links are dense and inline (cite sources, reference prior art, link docs)\n- `<details>` for code blocks that would break reading flow\n- Use `---` horizontal rules for major thematic breaks\n\n## Process\n\n1. Accept the user''s brain dump without requiring organization\n2. Read `references/voice-tone.md`\n3. Read 2-3 random example posts from `assets/` for tone calibration\n4. Read the reference files that match the post''s mode:\n   - Narrative arc → `references/story-circle.md`\n   - Personal/vulnerable → `references/emotional-personal.md`\n   - Fiction/parable → `references/fiction-mythic.md`\n   - Humor/satire → `references/humor-satire.md`\n   - Spiritual themes → `references/spirituality.md`\n5. Choose a structure pattern and draft\n6. Review: successive-paragraph rule, no corporate tone, voice matches examples\n7. Show draft to user and iterate\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-04T14:30:19.923Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Language Agents needing to emulate the Xe Iaso writing style for blog posts and narratives.","zh":"适合需要模拟Xe Iaso写作风格的语言代理，用于博客文章和叙事内容。","ja":"Xe Iasoの文章スタイルを模倣する必要がある言語エージェントに適しています。ブログ記事や物語に最適です。","ko":"Xe Iaso의 글쓰기 스타일을 모방해야 하는 언어 에이전트에게 적합합니다. 블로그 게시물 및 내러티브에 최적입니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Lenguaje que necesitan emular el estilo de escritura de Xe Iaso para publicaciones de blog y narrativas.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents de Langue ayant besoin d''émuler le style d''écriture de Xe Iaso pour les billets de blog et les récits.","de":"Perfekt für Sprachagenten, die den Schreibstil von Xe Iaso für Blog-Beiträge und Erzählungen emulieren müssen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Linguagem que precisam emular o estilo de escrita Xe Iaso para posts de blog e narrativas.","ru":"Идеально подходит для языковых агентов, которым необходимо имитировать стиль письма Xe Iaso для блог-постов и повествований.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء اللغويين الذين يحتاجون إلى محاكاة نمط كتابة Xe Iaso للمشاركات في المدونة والروايات."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to transform messy notes into coherent blog posts using narrative arc scaffolds and emotional register references, leveraging Markdown files like `references/voice-tone.md` and `references/story-circle.md` to calibrate tone and style.","zh":"赋予代理人使用叙事弧线脚手架和情感注册参考，利用Markdown文件（如`references/voice-tone.md`和`references/story-circle.md`）来校准语气和风格，将凌乱的笔记转化为连贯的博客文章的能力。","ja":"マークダウンファイル（例：`references/voice-tone.md`と`references/story-circle.md`）を利用して、物語のアークの脚手架や感情の登録リファレンスを使用して、整理されたブログ記事を作成する能力をエージェントに与えます。","ko":"_markdown 파일(예: `references/voice-tone.md` 및 `references/story-circle.md`)을 사용하여 내러티브 아크의 스캐폴딩과 감정 등록 참조를 활용하여 정리된 블로그 게시물 생성 기능을 에이전트에게 부여합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a transformar notas desorganizadas en publicaciones de blog coherentes utilizando andamios de arco narrativo y referencias de registro emocional, aprovechando archivos Markdown como `references/voice-tone.md` y `references/story-circle.md` para calibrar el tono y el estilo.","fr":"Permet aux agents de transformer des notes désorganisées en billets de blog cohérents en utilisant des échafaudages d''arc narratif et des références de registre émotionnel, en exploitant des fichiers Markdown tels que `references/voice-tone.md` et `references/story-circle.md` pour calibrer le ton et le style.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, unordentliche Notizen in kohärente Blog-Beiträge umzuwandeln, indem sie narrative Bogen-Schienen und emotionale Register-Referenzen verwenden, wobei Markdown-Dateien wie `references/voice-tone.md` und `references/story-circle.md` zur Kalibrierung von Ton und Stil genutzt werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a transformar notas desorganizadas em posts de blog coerentes usando estruturas de arco narrativo e referências de registro emocional, aproveitando arquivos Markdown como `references/voice-tone.md` e `references/story-circle.md` para calibrar o tom e o estilo.","ru":"Позволяет агентам преобразовывать неорганизованные заметки в связные блог-посты, используя нарративные арки и ссылки на эмоциональный регистр, используя файлы Markdown, такие как `references/voice-tone.md` и `references/story-circle.md`, для калибровки тона и стиля.","ar":"تمكن الوكلاء من تحويل الملاحظات المبعثرة إلى منشورات مدونة متسقة باستخدام هياكل القصة والمراجع التسجيلية العاطفية، واستخدام ملفات Markdown مثل `references/voice-tone.md` و `references/story-circle.md` لتعديل النبرة والنمط."},"useCases":{"en":["Generating blog posts with a consistent Xe Iaso tone","Transforming notes into narrative essays using the story circle scaffold","Calibrating emotional register for personal and vulnerable blog posts"],"zh":["使用一致的Xe Iaso语气生成博客文章","使用故事圆圈脚手架将笔记转化为叙事散文","使用情感注册来校准个人和脆弱的博客文章的语气"],"ja":["一貫したXe Iasoのトーンでブログ記事を生成する","ストーリーサークルの脚手架を使用してノートを物語エッセイに変換する","感情の登録を使用して個人的で脆弱なブログ記事のトーンを調整する"],"ko":["일관된 Xe Iaso의 어조로 블로그 게시물을 생성하는 것","스토리 원의 스캐폴딩을 사용하여 메모를 내러티브 에세이로 전환하는 것","감정 등록을 사용하여 개인적이고 취약한 블로그 게시물의 어조를 조정하는 것"],"es":["Generación de publicaciones de blog con un tono Xe Iaso coherente","Transformación de notas en ensayos narrativos utilizando el andamio del círculo de la historia","Calibración del registro emocional para publicaciones de blog personales y vulnerables"],"fr":["Génération de billets de blog avec un ton Xe Iaso cohérent","Transformation de notes en essais narratifs en utilisant l''échafaudage du cercle de l''histoire","Calibration du registre émotionnel pour des billets de blog personnels et vulnérables"],"de":["Erzeugung von Blog-Beiträgen mit einem konsistenten Xe Iaso-Ton","Umwandlung von Notizen in narrative Essays unter Verwendung des Story-Circle-Schienens","Kalibrierung des emotionalen Registers für persönliche und verletzliche Blog-Beiträge"],"pt":["Geração de posts de blog com um tom Xe Iaso consistente","Transformação de notas em ensaios narrativos usando a estrutura do círculo da história","Calibração do registro emocional para posts de blog pessoais e vulneráveis"],"ru":["Генерация блог-постов с постоянным тоном Xe Iaso","Преобразование заметок в нарративные эссе, используя структуру круга истории","Калибровка эмоционального регистра для личных и уязвимых блог-постов"],"ar":["إنشاء منشورات مدونة بطريقة موحدة لنمط Xe Iaso","تحويل الملاحظات إلى مقالات روائية باستخدام هيكل دائرة القصة","تعديل التسجيل العاطفي لمنشورات المدونة الشخصية والحساسة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to reference files like `references/voice-tone.md` and `assets/` example posts","Limited to generating content in the style of Xe Iaso","Needs manual calibration of tone through reading example posts"],"zh":["需要访问参考文件，如`references/voice-tone.md`和`assets/`示例帖子","仅限生成Xe Iaso风格的内容","需要通过阅读示例帖子手动校准语气"],"ja":["リファレンスファイル（例：`references/voice-tone.md`および`assets/`のサンプルポスト）へのアクセスが必要","Xe Iasoスタイルのコンテンツの生成のみ","サンプルポストを読むことで手動でトーンを調整する必要がある"],"ko":["참조 파일(예: `references/voice-tone.md` 및 `assets/` 샘플 게시물) 액세스가 필요합니다.","Xe Iaso 스타일의 콘텐츠 생성만 möglich","샘플 게시물을 읽어 수동으로 тон을 조정해야 합니다."],"es":["Requiere acceso a archivos de referencia como `references/voice-tone.md` y `assets/` publicaciones de ejemplo","Limitado a la generación de contenido en el estilo de Xe Iaso","Necesita una calibración manual del tono a través de la lectura de publicaciones de ejemplo"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès à des fichiers de référence tels que `references/voice-tone.md` et `assets/` publications d''exemple","Limité à la génération de contenu dans le style de Xe Iaso","Nécessite une calibration manuelle du ton via la lecture de publications d''exemple"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf Referenzdateien wie `references/voice-tone.md` und `assets/` Beispiel-Beiträge","Begrenzt auf die Erzeugung von Inhalten im Stil von Xe Iaso","Benötigt eine manuelle Kalibrierung des Tons durch das Lesen von Beispiel-Beiträgen"],"pt":["Requer acesso a arquivos de referência como `references/voice-tone.md` e `assets/` posts de exemplo","Limitado à geração de conteúdo no estilo de Xe Iaso","Necessita de calibração manual do tom por meio da leitura de posts de exemplo"],"ru":["Требует доступа к справочным файлам, таким как `references/voice-tone.md` и `assets/` примеры постов","Ограничен генерацией контента в стиле Xe Iaso","Требует ручной калибровки тона путем чтения примеров постов"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى ملفات مرجعية مثل `references/voice-tone.md` و `assets/` منشورات مثال","محدود بالمحتوى المُولَّد بنمط Xe Iaso","يحتاج إلى تعديل يدوي للنبرة من خلال قراءة منشورات مثال"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"978dfe2e2804884118e5ce49cf344478c326db34cf7195a45ae81b1a54e81dc9","qualityScore":49}');
